  "title": "India-US Trade and Investment Ties Revisited",
  "summary": "Piyush Goyal, India's Commerce and Industry Minister, is leading a business delegation to Japan to discuss ways to boost trade and investment ties, with the goal of expanding cooperation in high-technology manufacturing and next-generation industries. The visit is expected to assume significance as Japan set an investment target of 10 trillion yen in India over a decade. India and Canada reaffirm their commitment to finalize a Bilateral Investment Treaty and conclude trade negotiations by the end of 2026 to strengthen their economic ties.",
  "facts": [
